%main

  #hero
    .two-column
      %div
      
        %h1
          .span Pick-a-Pic
        %p
          Motivate
          %strong functional communication skills
          \ with an iPad app that is
          %strong easy to personalize
          \ for your learners.

      .div

        .video-frame
          %video{ autoplay: true, muted: true, loop: true }
            %source{ src: "/assets/video/speak-light.mp4", type: "video/mp4" }

  .one-column
    %h2
      Made for
      %strong your
      \ pictures

    %p
      Motivate your learner by using pictures of the exact things they want.
      %br
      With only a few taps, pictures can be imported from:
    
    %ul#import-list
      %li the Photos app
      %li the camera
      %li the Files app
      %li copied from the web
      %li text or emoji
      %li our gallery of examples

  %h2 Pick-a-Pic is for
  %h3 Early Communicators
  %p For learners that struggle with abstraction, Pick-a-Pic makes it easy to add pictures of the exact things they request.
  %h3 Caregivers
  %p Pick-a-Pic is designed to feel like the iPad apps that are used everyday, with a clear and intuitive interface.
  %h3 Professionals
  %p Behavior analysts and technicians can use Pick-a-Pic to implement functional communication training that is individualized and motivating to learners.
  %h3 Organizations
  %p Pick-a-Pic files can be synced and shared via iCloud and AirDrop so that learners have a consistent experience in any environment.

  %h2
    Pick-a-Pic is
    %em not
    for
  %p Pick-a-Pic is not meant for learners that are already able to effectively communicate in full sentences, and it is not meant to replace existing AAC apps. Pick-a-Pic is meant to springboard basic communication as one tool in a comprehensive and individualized AAC system, with learners graduating to more advanced apps when they are ready.


